    # If node a has left subtree containing b, then a is visited before b in pre-order (a < b)
    # In in-order traversal: b will be between a's left subtree nodes and right subtree nodes

    # The key: if a is parent of b or ancestor, and b is in left subtree, in in-order b < a
    # Our in-order output is just the node labels in in-order, which are their pre-order indices

